.TH CAU-MCP 1 "2026-11-02" "CAU EDR" "CAU EDR User Commands"
.SH NAME
cau\-mcp \- CAU EDR Model Context Protocol server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cau-mcp
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cau-mcp
exposes the same detection engine as
.BR cau (1)
over the Model Context Protocol: JSON-RPC 2.0, by default on standard input and
standard output. An MCP client (an LLM agent or an IDE) drives the engine
through bounded tools (scan, explain, draft and test rules, coverage), with file
access confined to the directories passed with \fB\-\-root\fP.
.PP
Resources are resolved with the same discovery rules as the scanner, so a
package install under \fB/usr\fP needs no configuration. The engine behind the
server is the scanner's, not a second implementation: the detectors, thresholds
and report formats are identical.
.PP
Without any \fB\-\-root\fP, the file-touching tools are disabled and only the
hash, rule and coverage tools remain available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-root " " \fIpath\fP
An allowed scan root for the file-touching tools. Repeatable. With no root,
file tools are disabled.
.TP
.BR \-db " " \fIfile\fR
The hash signature database. Auto-discovered when omitted. Unlike the scanner,
the server treats it as required and exits when it cannot be found.
.TP
.BR \-rules " " \fIfile\fR
The YARA rules file or directory. Auto-discovered when omitted; when YARA rules
are missing, YARA is disabled and the server continues.
.TP
.BR \-fuzzy\-db " " \fIfile\fR
The fuzzy-hash database (TLSH, ssdeep, imphash).
.TP
.BR \-max\-bytes " " \fIn\fR
Per-file size cap for file tools.
.TP
.BR \-max\-files " " \fIn\fR
Maximum files a single scan_dir call may enumerate.
.TP
.BR \-yara\-timeout " " \fIduration\fR
Per-file YARA scan budget (default 10s).
.TP
.BR \-http " " \fIaddress\fR
Serve the streamable-HTTP transport on this address (for example
\fB127.0.0.1:8923\fP) instead of stdio. Binding to a non-loopback address
exposes the scanner to everyone who can reach it, within the \fB\-\-root\fP
sandbox.
.TP
.BR \-no\-yara\fR, \fB\-no\-static\fR, \fB\-no\-stego\fR, \fB\-no\-encchain\fR, \fB\-no\-lnk\fR, \fB\-no\-ole\fR, \fB\-no\-pdf\fR, \fB\-no\-iso\fR, \fB\-no\-pkg\fR, \fB\-no\-peel\fR, \fB\-no\-heuristics\fR, \fB\-no\-fusion\fR
Disable one detector. A detector disabled by a flag is reported as disabled, not
silently skipped.
.TP
.BR \-version\fR
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The server ran and shut down cleanly.
.TP
.B 1
A startup failure: the signature database could not be loaded, the sandbox or
an explicit \fB\-\-rules\fP path was invalid, or the transport failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/cau/rules/*.yar
Bundled YARA rules.
.TP
.I /usr/share/cau/signatures/hashes.txt
Bundled hash signature database.
.TP
.I /usr/share/cau/signatures/fuzzy.txt
Bundled fuzzy-hash database.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR CAU_SIGNATURES ", " CAU_RULES ", " CAU_FUZZY
Default resource paths, as in
.BR cau (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
Serve to an MCP client, letting it scan a single directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cau-mcp \-\-root /srv/uploads \-\-db /usr/share/cau/signatures/hashes.txt
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cau (1)
